{
  "total": 40,
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f09682",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 3969,
      "bookHadithIndex": 1,
      "text": "Narrated Jabir ibn Abdullah: The Prophet (ﷺ) read the Qur'anic verse, \"And take ye the Station of Abraham as a place of prayer",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3969-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3969-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3969-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f09683",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 3970,
      "bookHadithIndex": 2,
      "text": "Narrated A'ishah:A man got up (for prayer) at night, he read the Qur'an and raised his voice in reading. When the morning came, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: May Allah have mercy on so-and-so! Last night he reminded me a number of verses which I was about to forget",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3970-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3970-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3970-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f09684",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 3971,
      "bookHadithIndex": 3,
      "text": "Narrated Abdullah ibn Abbas: The verse \"And no Prophet could (ever) be false to his trust\" was revealed about a red velvet. When it was found missing on the day of Badr, some people said; Perhaps the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) has taken it. So Allah, the Exalted, sent down \"And no prophet could (ever) be false to his trust\" to the end of the verse. Abu Dawud said: In the word yaghulla the letter ya has a short vowel a",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3971-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3971-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3971-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f09685",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 3972,
      "bookHadithIndex": 4,
      "text": "Anas b. Malik reported that Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) as saying:O Allah, I seek refuge in Thee from niggardliness and old age",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3972-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3972-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3972-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3972-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari (2823) Sahih Muslim (2706)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f09686",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 3973,
      "bookHadithIndex": 5,
      "text": "Narrated Laqit ibn Sabirah: I came in the deputation of Banu al-Muntafiq to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He then narrated the rest of the tradition. The Prophet (ﷺ) said: la tahsibanna (do not think) and did not say: la tahsabanna (do not think)",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3973-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3973-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3973-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f09687",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 3974,
      "bookHadithIndex": 6,
      "text": "Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:The Muslims met a man with some sheep of his. He said: Peace be upon you. But they killed him and took those few sheep. Thereupon the following Qur'anic verse was revealed: \"...And say to anyone who offers you a salutation: Thou art none of believer, coveting the perishable good of this life.\" meaning these few sheep",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3974-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3974-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3974-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3974-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari (4591) Sahih Muslim (3025)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f09688",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 3975,
      "bookHadithIndex": 7,
      "text": "Narrated Zayd ibn Thabit: The Prophet (ﷺ) used to read: \"Not equal are those believers who sit (at home) and receive no hurt (ghayru ulid-darari) but the narrator Sa'id did not say the words \"used to read",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3975-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3975-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3975-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f09689",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 3976,
      "bookHadithIndex": 8,
      "text": "Narrated Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) read the verse: \"eye for eye\" (al-'aynu bil-'ayn)",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3976-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3976-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3976-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f0968a",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 3977,
      "bookHadithIndex": 9,
      "text": "Narrated Anas ibn Malik: The Prophet (ﷺ) read the verse: \"We ordained therein for them: Life for life and eye for eye (an-nafsa bin-nafsi wal-'aynu bil-'ayn)",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3977-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3977-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3977-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3977-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f0968b",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 3978,
      "bookHadithIndex": 10,
      "text": "Narrated Abdullah ibn Umar: Atiyyah ibn Sa'd al-Awfi said: I recited to Abdullah ibn Umar the verse: \"It is Allah Who created you in a state of (helplessness) weakness (min da'f).\" He said: (Read) min du'f. I recited it to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) as you recited it to me, and he gripped me as I gripped you",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3978-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3978-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3978-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3978-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f0968c",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 3979,
      "bookHadithIndex": 11,
      "text": "Narrated AbuSa'id al-Khudri: The Prophet (ﷺ) read the verse mentioned above, \"min du'f",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3979-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3979-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3979-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3979-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f0968d",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 3980,
      "bookHadithIndex": 12,
      "text": "Narrated Ubayy b. Ka'b:\"Say, in the bounty of Allah, and in His mercy- in that let you rejoice",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3980-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3980-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3980-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3980-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f0968e",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 3981,
      "bookHadithIndex": 13,
      "text": "(Narrated Ibn Abzi: Ubayy ibn Ka'b) said: The Prophet (ﷺ) read the verse: \"Say: In the bounty of Allah and in His mercy--in that let you rejoice: that is better than the wealth you hoard",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3981-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3981-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3981-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f0968f",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 3982,
      "bookHadithIndex": 14,
      "text": "Narrated Asma' daughter of Yazid: She heard the Prophet (ﷺ) read the verse: \"He acted unrighteously.\" (innahu 'amila ghayra salih)",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3982-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3982-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3982-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f09690",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 3983,
      "bookHadithIndex": 15,
      "text": "Narrated Umm Salamah, Ummul Mu'minin: Shahr ibn Hawshab said: I asked Umm Salamah: How did the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) read this verse: \"For his conduct is unrighteous (innahu 'amalun ghayru salih\". She replied: He read it: \"He acted unrighteously\" (innahu 'amila ghayra salih). Abu Dawud said: This tradition has been transmitted by Harun al-Nahwi and Musa b. Khalaf from Thabit as reported by the narrator 'Abd al-Aziz",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3983-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3983-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3983-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3983-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f09691",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 3984,
      "bookHadithIndex": 16,
      "text": "Narrated Ubayy ibn Ka'b:: When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prayed, he began with himself and said: May the mercy of Allah be upon us and upon Moses. If he had patience, he would have seen marvels from his Companion. But he said: \"(Moses) said: If ever I ask thee about anything after this, keep me not in they company: then wouldst thou have received (full) excuse from my side\". Hamzah lengthened it",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3984-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3984-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3984-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3984-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f09692",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 3985,
      "bookHadithIndex": 17,
      "text": "Narrated Ubayy ibn Ka'b: The Prophet (ﷺ) read the Qur'anic verse: \"Thou hast received (full) excuse from me (min ladunni)\" and put tashdid (doubling of consonants) on nun (n)",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3985-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3985-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3985-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3985-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f09693",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 3986,
      "bookHadithIndex": 18,
      "text": "Narrated Abdullah ibn Abbas: Ubayy ibn Ka'b made me read the following verse as the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) made him read: \"in a spring of murky water\" (fi 'aynin hami'atin) with short vowel a after h",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3986-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3986-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3986-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f09694",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 3987,
      "bookHadithIndex": 19,
      "text": "Narrated AbuSa'id al-Khudri: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: A man from the Illiyyun will look downwards at the people of Paradise and Paradise will be glittering as if it were a brilliant star. He (the narrator) said: In this way the word durri (brilliant) occurs in this tradition, i.e. the letter dal (d) has short vowel u and it has no hamzah ('). AbuBakr and Umar will be of them and will have some additional blessings",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3987-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3987-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3987-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f09695",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 3988,
      "bookHadithIndex": 20,
      "text": "Narrated Farwah ibn Musayk al-Ghutayfi: I came to the Prophet (ﷺ). He then narrated the rest of the tradition. A man from the people said: \"Messenger of Allah! tell us about Saba'; what is it: land or woman? He replied: It is neither land nor woman; it is a man to whom ten children of the Arabs were born: six of them lived in the Yemen and four lived in Syria. The narrator Uthman said al-Ghatafani instead of al-Ghutayfi. He said: It has been transmitted to us by al-Hasan ibn al-Hakam an-Nakha'i",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3988-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3988-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Hasan Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3988-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f09696",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 3989,
      "bookHadithIndex": 21,
      "text": "Narrated Abu Hurairah:The Prophet (ﷺ) as saying - the narrator Isma'il transmitted it from Abu Hurairah, and mentioned the tradition about the coming down of revelation-: \"So far (is this the case) that when terror is removed from their hearts",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3989-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3989-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3989-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari (4800، 4701)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f09697",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 3990,
      "bookHadithIndex": 22,
      "text": "Narrated Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (ﷺ): The reading of the following verse by the Prophet (ﷺ) goes: \"Nay, but there came to thee (ja'atki) my signs, and thou didst reject them (fakadhdhabti biha) ; thou wast haughty (wastakbarti) and became one of those who reject Faith (wa kunti). Abu Dawud said: This is a mursal tradition, i.e. the link of the Companion has been omitted, for the narrator al-Rabi' did not meet Umm Salamah",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3990-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3990-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Daif Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3990-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3990-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f09698",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 3991,
      "bookHadithIndex": 23,
      "text": "Narrated Aisha, Ummul Mu'minin: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) read: \"(There is for him) Rest and satisfaction\" (faruhun wa rayhan)",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3991-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3991-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3991-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3991-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f09699",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 3992,
      "bookHadithIndex": 24,
      "text": "Safwan b. Ya'la quoting his father said:I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) read on the pulpit the verse: \"They will cry: O Malik.\" Abu Dawud said: That is, without shortening the name (Malik)",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3992-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3992-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3992-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari (4819) Sahih Muslim (871)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f0969a",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 3993,
      "bookHadithIndex": 25,
      "text": "Narrated Abdullah ibn Mas'ud: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) made me read the verse \"It is I who give (all) sustenance, Lord of power, steadfast (for ever)",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3993-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3993-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3993-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f0969b",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 3994,
      "bookHadithIndex": 26,
      "text": "Narrated Abdullah ibn Mas'ud: The Prophet (ﷺ) used to read the verse \"Is there any that will receive admonition (muddakir)? \" that is with doubling of consonant [(dal)(d)]. Abu Dawud said: The word muddakir may be pronounced as mim (m) with a short vowel u. (dal)(d) with a short vowel and kaf (k) with a short vowel i",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3994-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3994-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3994-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f0969c",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 3995,
      "bookHadithIndex": 27,
      "text": "Narrated Jabir ibn Abdullah: I saw the Prophet (ﷺ) reading the verse; \"does he think that his wealth would make him last for ever?",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3995-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3995-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Daif Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3995-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Isnaad Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f0969d",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 3996,
      "bookHadithIndex": 28,
      "text": "Narrated Abu Qilabah:That the Prophet (ﷺ) made a man read the verse: \"For, that day His chastisement will be such as none (else) can be chastised. And his bonds will be such as none (other) can be bound. Abu Dawud said: According to some (scholars), there is a narrator between the narrator Khalid and Abu Qilabah",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3996-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3996-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Daif Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3996-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f0969e",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 3997,
      "bookHadithIndex": 29,
      "text": "Narrated Abu Qilabah: A man whom the Prophet (ﷺ) made the following verse read informed me, or he was informed by a man whom a man made the following verse read through a man whom the Prophet (ﷺ) made the following verse read: \"For, that day His chastisement will be such as none (else) can be inflicted (la yu'adhdhabu) Abu Dawud said: 'Asim, al-A'mash, Talhah b. Musarrif, Abu Ja'far Yazid b. al-Qa'qa', Shaibah b. Nassah, Nafi' b. 'Abd al-Rahman, 'Abd Allah b. Kathir al-Dari, Abu 'Amr b. al-'Ala', Hamzat al-Zayyat, 'Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj, Qatadah, al-Hasan al-Basri, Mujahid, Hamid al=A'raj, Abd Allah b. 'Abbas and 'Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Bakr recited: \"For,that day His chastisement will be such as none (else) can inflict (la ya'adhdhibu), and His bonds will be such as none (other) can bind (wa la yathiqu), except the verse mentioned in this tradition from the Prophet (ﷺ). It has een read yu'adhdhabu with short vowel a in passive voice",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3997-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3997-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Daif Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3997-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Hasan"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f0969f",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 3998,
      "bookHadithIndex": 30,
      "text": "Narrated AbuSa'id al-Khudri: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) related a tradition in which he mentioned the words \"Jibril and Mikal\" and he pronounced them \"Jibra'ila wa Mika'ila.\" Abu Dawud said: Khalaf said: I did not put the pen aside from writing letters (huruf) for forty years: nothing tired me (or made me incapable of writing), even Jibril and Mika'il did not tire me",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3998-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3998-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Daif Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3998-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f096a0",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 3999,
      "bookHadithIndex": 31,
      "text": "Narrated AbuSa'id al-Khudri: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) mentioned the name of the one who will sound the trumpet (sahib as-sur) and said: On his right will be Jibra'il and on his left will be Mika'il",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3999-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3999-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Daif"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-3999-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f096a1",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 4000,
      "bookHadithIndex": 32,
      "text": "Narrated Ibn al-Musayyab: The Prophet (ﷺ), AbuBakr, Umar and Uthman used to read \"maliki yawmid-din (master of the Day of Judgment)\". The first to read maliki yawmid-din was Marwan. Abu Dawud said: This is sounder that the tradition which transmitted by al-Zuhri from Anas, and al-Zuhri from Salim, from his father (Ibn 'Umar)",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-4000-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Daif Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-4000-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Daif Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-4000-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f096a2",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 4001,
      "bookHadithIndex": 33,
      "text": "Narrated Umm Salamah, Ummul Mu'minin: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to recite: \"In the name of Allah, the Cherisher and Sustainer of the worlds; most Gracious, most Merciful; Master of the Day of Judgment,\" breaking its recitation into verses, one after another. Abu Dawud said: I heard Ahmad (b. Hanbal) say: The early reading is: Maliki yawmi'l-din",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-4001-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-4001-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-4001-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Daif"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f096a3",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 4002,
      "bookHadithIndex": 34,
      "text": "Narrated Abu Dharr:I was sitting behind the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) who was riding a donkey while the sun was setting. He asked: Do you know where this sets ? I replied: Allah and his Apostle know best. He said: It sets in a spring of warm water (Hamiyah)",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-4002-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-4002-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih Isnaad"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-4002-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari (3199، 4802، 4803) Sahih Muslim (159)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f096a4",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 4003,
      "bookHadithIndex": 35,
      "text": "Narrated Ibn al-Asqa':The Prophet (ﷺ) came to them in the swelling place of immigrants and a man asked him: Which is the greatest verse of the Qur'an ? The Prophet (ﷺ) replied: Allah, there is no god but He - the Living, the Self-Subsisting Eternal. No slumber can seize Him nor sleep",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-4003-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-4003-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-4003-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih Lighairihi"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-4003-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f096a5",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 4004,
      "bookHadithIndex": 36,
      "text": "Narrated Shariq:Ibn Mas'ud said read the verse: \"Now come, thou\" (haita laka). Then Shariq said: We read it, \"hi'tu laka\" (I am prepared for thee). Ibn Mas'ud said: I read it as I have been taught ; it is dearer to me",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-4004-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-4004-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-4004-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-4004-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih Bukhari (4692)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f096a6",
      "editionId": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320",
      "bookIndex": 32,
      "hadithIndex": 4005,
      "bookHadithIndex": 37,
      "text": "Narrated Shariq:'Abd Allah (b. Mas'ud) was told that the people had read this verse: \"She said: Now come, thou\" (hita laka). He said: I read it as I have been taught ; it is dearer to me. It goes \"wa qalat haita laka\" (She said: Now come thou)",
      "grades": [
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-4005-alalbani",
          "name": "Al-Albani",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-4005-muhammadmuhyialdinabdulhamid",
          "name": "Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-4005-shuaibalarnaut",
          "name": "Shuaib Al Arnaut",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        },
        {
          "id": "69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1320-32-4005-zubairalizai",
          "name": "Zubair Ali Zai",
          "grade": "Sahih"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "69b6c59add1a4c9c86f096a7",
